eparation relies entirely on the executor trace and the single before/after-executor snapshot pair.\",\"Temporary memhog test files were not explicitly deleted by the executor before the reboot; their absence in the after-executor snapshot is attributable to the reboot clearing /tmp rather than an explicit cleanup action, though no residue remains in the final state.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"inventory-api runs as a systemd-managed service on node1 and serves traffic","status":"satisfied","summary":"app.py and inventory-api.service were created, enabled, and started; systemctl reports active, and curl to /health and /inventory returned correct JSON responses.","evidence_ids":["cmd-810b0534683e45e2","cmd-d847ed7259284885"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Service is configured to be spared by the kernel OOM killer","status":"satisfied","summary":"The running inventory-api process (PID 1311) had /proc/PID/oom_score_adj = -1000 via OOMScoreAdjust=-1000 in the unit file, directly confirming OOM protection was applied.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ed446218bfd24a2f"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"A genuine memory-hungry process drives the node out of memory","status":"satisfied","summary":"A background memhog.py process was launched and memory usage climbed to 1.9Gi/1.9Gi used with only 52Mi free and no swap, directly demonstrating real memory exhaustion (not simulated).","evidence_ids":["cmd-5c1ee33f4e034042","cmd-6f17391f07614a57"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Kernel OOM killer selects and kills the memory hog rather than inventory-api","status":"satisfied","summary":"dmesg shows 'Out of memory: Killed process 1392 (python3) ... oom_score_adj:0', matching the memhog PID, while inventory-api (oom_score_adj:-1000) was confirmed still active and untouched.","evidence_ids":["cmd-44b7e48d9a40462d"]},{"id":"req-5","requirement":"inventory-api continues serving requests throughout and after the OOM event","status":"satisfied","summary":"Post